"82" y="235" style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase" fill="var(--steel)">03</text><text x="118" y="237" style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.01em" fill="var(--ink)">Running</text><text x="82" y="259" style="font-family:var(--body);font-size:10.5px" fill="var(--steel)">One workflow live, behind a gate.</text></g><g class="climb-stage" style="--i:3"><rect class="climb-plate" x="62" y="279" width="458" height="74"></rect><line class="climb-rung" x1="30" y1="316" x2="62" y2="316" stroke="var(--line)"></line><rect class="climb-node" x="25" y="311" width="10" height="10" transform="rotate(45 30 316)"></rect><text x="82" y="310" style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase" fill="var(--steel)">04</text><text x="118" y="312" style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:17px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.01em" fill="var(--ink)">Native</text><text x="82" y="334" style="font-family:var(--body);font-size:10.5px" fill="var(--steel)">Your team builds the next one.</text></g><g class="climb-head"><rect x="26" y="22" width="8" height="8" transform="rotate(45 30 26)" fill="var(--ink)"></rect></g><rect x="26" y="406" width="8" height="8" transform="rotate(45 30 410)" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--steel)"></rect><text x="62" y="414" style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase" fill="var(--ink)">AI native<tspan fill="var(--steel)"> · Yours to run</tspan></text></svg></div></div></header><section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><h2>What changes, and where.</h2><p class="intro">Transformation is not a model licence. It happens in three places at once, and skipping any one of them is why most of it stalls.</p><div class="layers"><div class="layer"><p class="n">Layer 01</p><h3>People</h3><p>We deploy the POD operating model into your team, working on your systems and your rules to unlock the organizational intelligence you already have. Your people learn the framework while it is being built. By the end they are building the next agent on it themselves.</p></div><div class="layer"><p class="n">Layer 02</p><h3>Product</h3><p>Agents wired into the systems you already run, acting on live transactions. Nothing is re-platformed: the agents are infused into the products your team already works in. The approvals they stop at happen on the platform we stand up with you.</p></div><div class="layer"><p class="n">Layer 03</p><h3>Process</h3><p>Agentic workflow that runs on the rules your business already follows: your approval thresholds, your escalation paths, your guardrails. Encoded, audited and governed rather than reinvented, so the agents work on top of the framework you have.</p></div></div><div class="fold-close"><p>Six agents already run on this model. Review one against your own process, or take it as the starting point for the agent you actually need.</p><a class="btn" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/contact' ) ); ?>">Book a discovery call</a></div></div></section><section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><h2 class="problem-h">You bought AI. Nothing does the work.</h2><p class="intro">You have tried the obvious fixes. None of them touched the real problem.</p><ol class="problems"><li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>You bought the tools.</h3><p>Licences for copilots and assistants. A few enthusiasts got faster. Everyone else kept re-keying invoices by hand. The seats renew whether or not anyone signs in.</p></div></li><li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>You hired the engineers.</h3><p>Headcount went up. Throughput did not. They are good people maintaining demos, because nothing they built was ever allowed near a system of record.</p></div></li><li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>You paid for frontier models.</h3><p>Real spend on tokens for pilots that never left the sandbox. Nobody would let a model touch a live transaction. So it never touched one.</p></div></li><li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div><h3>Your best people are stuck on it.</h3><p>The engineers you can least afford to lose are debugging prompts and rewriting evaluation scripts. That is precisely the work this was meant to absorb.</p></div></li><li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">05</span><div><h3>Nobody has seen the value.</h3><p>No line on the P&amp;L moved. The board asks about AI and the honest answer is still a roadmap. Two years in, that answer is getting expensive.</p></div></li></ol><p class="problem-closer">The problem was never the model, and it was never your team. <span class="hl">Nothing was wired to a system of record, and nothing had permission to act.</span></p><div class="fold-close"><p>That is the part we fix, and it is the only part that turns a pilot into a payable outcome.</p><a class="btn" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/contact' ) ); ?>">Book a discovery call</a></div></div></section><section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><h2>Execution made better, not rebuilt.</h2><p class="intro">We do not re-platform your business. Your ERP stays where it is, your team stays who they are, and your processes keep the judgment that makes them work. What changes is how much of the execution a person has to do by hand.</p><div class="layers solution-cards"><div class="layer"><span class="l-icon"><svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="1.5" y="1.5" width="27" height="27" stroke-dasharray="3 3"></rect><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></rect></svg></span><h3>Embedded, not advising</h3><p>Our engineers work inside your team, on your tickets, in your standups. You get people who ship, not a deck and a follow-up.</p></div><div class="layer"><span class="l-icon"><svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 2 V28"></path><path d="M4 8 H22"></path><path d="M4 15 H27"></path><path d="M4 22 H17"></path></svg></span><h3>Fluent in your process</h3><p>The pricing exception nobody documented. The customer who always gets a call first. That accumulated judgment is your advantage, and it stays yours.</p></div><div class="layer"><span class="l-icon"><svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="miter" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 26 H9 V18 H15"></path><path d="M15 18 H21 V10 H28" stroke-dasharray="3 3"></path><rect x="12.2" y="15.2" width="5.6" height="5.6" transform="rotate(45 15 18)" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></rect></svg></span><h3>Built to be handed over</h3><p>The platform runs in your environment and the runbooks are yours. Step four exists so your engineers build the next agent without us.</p></div></div><div class="guarantee"><p class="h">The commitment</p><p class="g-head">If the number does not move, you do not pay.</p><p class="g-body">We agree what we are measuring before anything is built, against a baseline taken during the assessment.</p><p class="g-note">Metric, baseline and threshold are written down in step one, so nobody is arguing about the definition at invoice time.</p></div><div class="fold-close"><p>This is the same shape as a via ferrata. Someone bolts the line into the rock; everyone else crosses on their own feet.</p><a class="btn" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/contact' ) ); ?>">Book a discovery call</a></div></div></section><section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><h2>Agents already doing the work.</h2><p class="intro">Six agents built and running against real transactions. These are examples of what gets built, not a catalogue you pick from, and every one is rebuilt around how your business actually operates.</p><div class="crew"><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/sterling' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Sterling</h3></span><p class="role">Working capital</p><ul><li>Daily cash position, written not charted</li><li>Collections ranked by recovery odds</li><li>Disputed invoices held back automatically</li><li>Promise-to-pay tracked to the date</li></ul><span class="go">How Sterling works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/clark' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Clark</h3></span><p class="role">Payables</p><ul><li>Any format: PDF, scan, portal or email body</li><li>Duplicate and near-duplicate detection</li><li>Three-way match with tolerance rules</li><li>Coding proposed from history, not guessed</li></ul><span class="go">How Clark works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/tally' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Tally</h3></span><p class="role">Reconciliation</p><ul><li>Runs continuously, not at month-end</li><li>Variance commentary drafted for review</li><li>Accrual proposals with support attached</li><li>Break aging, so nothing sits unexplained</li></ul><span class="go">How Tally works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/chandler' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Chandler</h3></span><p class="role">Procurement</p><ul><li>Multi-vendor RFQ across channels</li><li>Contract terms extracted and monitored</li><li>Price variance flagged against schedule</li><li>Award recommendation with the math shown</li></ul><span class="go">How Chandler works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/swift' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Swift</h3></span><p class="role">Order management</p><ul><li>PO document to sales order in minutes</li><li>Pricing and terms validated on intake</li><li>Only true exceptions routed to a person</li><li>Acknowledgement sent the same hour</li></ul><span class="go">How Swift works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/quill' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Quill</h3></span><p class="role">Quotes &amp; CRM</p><ul><li>Every enquiry read, none dropped</li><li>Priced against your own rule set</li><li>Drafted in the CRM, ready to edit</li><li>Follow-up scheduled and tracked</li></ul><span class="go">How Quill works →</span></a></div><div class="bespoke"><h3>Your agents are built around your organization.</h3><p>The way you price, route, approve and escalate is years of accumulated judgment, and it's a real advantage. It belongs to you and it stays with you, we're not asking you to hand over your playbook or fit yourself into someone else's template. We start from how your business already works, encode that logic into agents built for your environment, and leave you with an operation that runs faster with exactly the things that make you good at it still intact.</p></div><p class="note">Every agent stops at an approval gate until it has earned its way out of one. Nothing releases cash, commits spend or touches a customer without a person saying so.</p><div class="fold-close"><p>Every one of them stops at a person before it reaches a customer. Open any agent to see exactly where that line sits.</p><a class="btn" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/contact' ) ); ?>">Book a discovery call</a></div></div></section><section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Systems of record</p><h2>SAP first, because that's where the work is.</h2><p class="intro">Our deepest work is against SAP HANA, reading the ledger live, transforming it, and writing back through the same controls your team already uses. Two of our recent deployments started there. Everything else on this list connects too, and the agents don't care which of them holds the data.</p><div class="marq"><div class="marq-track"><span class="marq-item primary">SAP HANA</span><span class="marq-item primary">SAP S/4HANA</span><span class="marq-item">NetSuite</span><span class="marq-item">Dynamics 365</span><span class="marq-item">Salesforce</span><span class="marq-item">HubSpot</span><span class="marq-item">Snowflake</span><span class="marq-item">Databricks</span><span class="marq-item">Azure</span><span class="marq-item">AWS</span><span class="marq-item">SharePoint</span><span class="marq-item">OneDrive</span><span class="marq-item">Outlook</span><span class="marq-item">Gmail</span><span class="marq-item">Slack</span><span class="marq-item">Teams</span><span class="marq-item">Power BI</span><span class="marq-item">Coupa</span><span class="marq-item">Concur</span><span class="marq-item">Stripe</span><span class="marq-item">Xero</span><span class="marq-item">Jira</span><span class="marq-item">ServiceNow</span><span class="marq-item">EDI</span><span aria-hidden="true" style="display:contents"><span class="marq-item primary">SAP HANA</span><span class="marq-item primary">SAP S/4HANA</span><span class="marq-item">NetSuite</span><span class="marq-item">Dynamics 365</span><span class="marq-item">Salesforce</span><span class="marq-item">HubSpot</span><span class="marq-item">Snowflake</span><span class="marq-item">Databricks</span><span class="marq-item">Azure</span><span class="marq-item">AWS</span><span class="marq-item">SharePoint</span><span class="marq-item">OneDrive</span><span class="marq-item">Outlook</span><span class="marq-item">Gmail</span><span class="marq-item">Slack</span><span class="marq-item">Teams</span><span class="marq-item">Power BI</span><span class="marq-item">Coupa</span><span class="marq-item">Concur</span><span class="marq-item">Stripe</span><span class="marq-item">Xero</span><span class="marq-item">Jira</span><span class="marq-item">ServiceNow</span><span class="marq-item">EDI</span></span></div></div></div></section><section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><h2>How the engagement runs.</h2><p class="intro">Four stages from absent to native. The line goes in before anyone climbs, and your team ends up able to walk the route without us.</p><div class="stages"><div class="stage"><p class="n">01</p><h3>Assess</h3><p class="dur">2 weeks</p><p class="d">We map workflows, not org charts. You get a ranked list of candidate workflows with a defensible number attached to each, whether or not you go further with us.</p></div><div class="stage"><p class="n">02</p><h3>Anchor the platform</h3><p class="dur">3 weeks</p><p class="d">We stand up the platform in your environment, frontier models, open-weight, or both, depending on what your data residency and cost profile demand.</p></div><div class="stage"><p class="n">03</p><h3>First agent live</h3><p class="dur">Under 90 days</p><p class="d">One agent, one workflow, in production against real transactions with a human approval gate on every action.</p></div><div class="stage"><p class="n">04</p><h3>Expand, then hand over</h3><p class="dur">Ongoing</p><p class="d">Add agents as trust builds. When you want it in-house, we install the POD operating model with runbooks and evaluation harnesses documented.</p></div></div><p class="more"><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/how-it-works' ) ); ?>">Read the full engagement model →</a></p></div></section><section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><h2>Operators, not an agency.</h2><p class="intro">We ran the technology organisation through exactly this kind of transformation, with a P&amp;L attached and a board asking about the number. Everything below came out of operating, not advising.</p><div class="proof"><div><p class="fig">$1.2B</p><p class="cap">Total GMV scaled across the platform and products we built</p></div><div><p class="fig">120+</p><p class="cap">Real-world FTEs of capacity unlocked, and counting</p></div><div><p class="fig">25 → 5</p><p class="cap">Days to close the books, with a reconciliation agent on it</p></div><div><p class="fig">30%</p><p class="cap">Improvement in AR collection times</p></div></div><p class="more"><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/about' ) ); ?>">More on how we work →</a></p></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="wrap"><h2>Bring us one workflow.</h2><p>Thirty minutes, no deck. Pick the process that costs you most in people, errors or delay, and we'll pressure-test whether an agent is genuinely the right answer for it.</p><ul class="cta-list"><li>An honest read on whether that workflow is a good agent candidate</li><li>What the first deployment would involve, and roughly what it costs</li><li>An honest answer if the sequencing is wrong and you should fix something else first</li></ul><a class="btn btn-lg" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/contact' ) ); ?>">Book a discovery call</a></div></section>
